What is Organic Zinc Reagent?
Aromatic and aliphatic zinc salts featuring a direct carbon‑zinc bond represent a unique class of organometallic intermediates. Their ability to mediate cross‑coupling, addition and stereocontrolled transformations under comparatively mild conditions makes them attractive for synthetic chemists operating in a high‑purity environment.
